  "terms": {
    "title": "Terms of Service",
    "btn_accept": "I Understand and Accept",
    "p1_title": "1. Use of the Talk-me Platform",
    "p1_text": "Talk-me is an offline communication tool, voice transmission via processed WebRTC protocol and network telemetry. It is strictly designed for professional use in acoustic shows, live production, and isolated deployments (\"Zero-Cloud\"). Its operation under insecure, WAN, or open networks falls under the sole responsibility of the network administrator.",
    "p2_title": "2. Intelligent Voice Processing (Local AI)",
    "p2_text": "The Artificial Intelligence engine (Vosk) executes 100% local diction recognition mathematical models on the central node's CPU. The user consents to their voice being captured by the microphone (\"AudioWorklet Node\"), mathematically transformed into low-frequency PCM blocks (16kHz), and transmitted to the primary server for instant processing. All semantic processing occurs within the Intranet.",
    "p3_title": "3. Privacy and Absence of External Databases",
    "p3_text": "Privacy is the cornerstone of this architecture by design. Talk-me lacks connections to Third-Party Clouds, commercial analytical biometric systems, or persistent cloud databases. Audio packets (ArrayBuffer Blob PCM) or commands (OSC) expire once received. Semantic dictionaries are saved locally.",
    "p4_title": "4. Use of Browser APIs (\"Browser Injections\")",
    "p4_text": "By accepting this service, you allow Talk-me to invoke operating system notifications (`Notification API`), manipulate speaker devices (`sinkId`), or activate local physical actuators using the flashlight (`MediaTrackConstraints`) and haptic vibration motors (`Navigator.Vibrate`) to guarantee red alerts.",
    "p5_title": "5. Disclaimer on Hardware Control",
    "p5_text": "The \"Triggers\" system authorizes the direct insertion of physical bidirectional commands to the native MIDI bus or via Binary OSC UDP Injections to third-party consoles. The developer is not responsible for collateral damage derived from erroneous trigger configurations."
  },
